{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["The reason for mentioning the ovot and yid'onim: on account of the dead. So it is written in Isaiah, 'on behalf of the living, to the dead.' <b>The ovot.</b> From the root of וכאובות חדשים (Isaiah 65:3), for they are the essence of this craft." "<b>And the yid'onim.</b> From the root of דעת (knowledge), that they seek to know the future. The empty-headed said: were the ovot not true as well, a way of sorcery, Scripture would not have forbidden them. And I say the opposite of their words, for Scripture did not forbid truth, only falsehood and the testimony of the idolatrous images. And were it not that I do not wish to lengthen, I would explain the matter of the woman with the ov at Endor with complete proofs." "The sense of <b>do not turn to</b>: to one who knows the craft." "The sense of <b>do not seek</b>: to inquire of." "The sense of <b>I am YHWH your Elohim</b>: that you should not seek anything but HaShem alone. And behold, He declared it impure, for the soul that turns and seeks is impure, for it does not cleave to HaShem."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:16.902122906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}